    "commit": "232a7255fe883cfc51f18d7c2bdcf697da085421",
    "commit_body": "Gradient dampener targeting calls (overall>=75) where the stochastic component\nis below neutral AND the weekly adjustment is weakly positive. These signals\nfire on trend/volume dominance while stoch contradicts \u2014 miss at +3.7pp above\nbaseline (z=+4.5, N=3,379, 46% of 75+ calls; 5y v32 ledger).\n\nMechanism (gradient, no hard gate):\n  stoch_w  = clip((35 - stoch) / 35, 0, 1)  -- 0 at neutral=35, 1 at stoch=0\n  wadj_w   = clip((12 - wadj)  / 11, 0, 1)  -- 0 at wadj=12, 1 at wadj=1\n  weakness = stoch_w * wadj_w\n  overall -= 0.30 * weakness * (overall - 55)\n\nCalibrated via 175-variant gradient Bayesian sweep (stoch_wadj_bayes.py v2):\n56/175 pass H1+H3+H4+H5. Winner: sn=35 (COMP_BINS anchor), wg=12, K=0.30.\nPer-tier 5y: 85+ +1.80pp, 80+ +1.17pp, 75+ +0.93pp. N drops -12 to -14%\n(within H3 +-15%). Puts unchanged (H4). Sign-consistent 1y/3y/5y (H5).\n\nComplements CWCF (v32, handles wadj<1); clean handoff at wadj=1.0 -- same\nsignal cannot trigger both. Exposes weight_info['cswc_dampen'] for explain-scores.\n\nAlso: CLAUDE.md -- mandatory order warning for ALGORITHM_VERSION + code commits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
    "commit_short": "232a7255",
    "commit_subject": "v34 scoring: call stoch-weekly contradiction dampener (CSWC)",
